  "diagnosis": [
    "Exactly shared curved geometry cancels under independent SVG rendering. Remaining measured Viking hairlines lie between distinct near-coincident cuts.",
    "The ordinary sharing gate compares 256-pixel masks and a 512-pixel enlargement of that coarse target before inspecting the original source. Some source-improving valid joins are rejected by these coarse quantized scores.",
    "Simply resizing the original mask directly at 512 does not fix every case: pixel-center classification can disagree even with the independent 800-pixel render.",
    "Averaging the existing continuous boundary objective in both orientations gives an improvement at 512 and 1024 rows for every inspected valid blocked join. This is a numerical area approximation, not an exact discrete-pixel derivative."
